=== T3.6: the LK gradient covariance -- fused against composed ===
target: aarch64 -- AUTHORITATIVE (the reference device is where this closes)
640x480, 200 keypoints, one window each -- the LK access pattern of
ARCHITECTURE 7.5. The rule this is measured against is in this file's
header, written before measuring.

"composed/fused" > 1.00x means the FUSED entry point T3.6 ships is faster,
confirming D-15 axis 2 at this level. "plane/4arg" > 1.00x means the
precomputed selector plane is faster than the four-argument form -- which it
is expected to be, and is the speed T3.6 spends to save the plane.

  word      W           fused     composed   composed/  fused+plane   comp+plane      plane/       spread f / c
                    ns/window    ns/window       fused    ns/window    ns/window        4arg
  uint32_t  7           226.9        296.9       1.31x        163.1        240.6       1.39x      4.1% / 3.8%
  uint32_t  15          452.6        540.0       1.19x        351.5        465.8       1.29x      0.8% / 4.2%
  uint32_t  31          945.7       1108.9       1.17x        789.3       1004.0       1.20x      0.8% / 1.5%

  word      W           fused     composed   composed/  fused+plane   comp+plane      plane/       spread f / c
                    ns/window    ns/window       fused    ns/window    ns/window        4arg
  uint64_t  7           217.3        268.8       1.24x        150.6        248.5       1.44x      1.3% / 2.0%
  uint64_t  15          435.1        476.4       1.10x        314.7        436.0       1.38x      1.5% / 1.2%
  uint64_t  31          857.6        937.3       1.09x        671.8        852.4       1.28x      0.8% / 0.6%

  MEMORY (uint32_t), beyond the four derivative planes every form reads.
  "allocs/pass" is operator new calls COUNTED over one pass of 200 windows
  at W=31 -- the 0 B is a measurement of this binary, not a printed claim.
  (counter self-check: plain new counted 1, over-aligned new counted 1; both must be 1)
                       scratch  allocs/pass
    fused                  0 B            0      <- T3.6 SHIPS THIS
    composed               0 B            0
    fused+plane        38400 B            0      one sign_x^sign_y plane at 640x480
    composed+plane     38400 B            0
    A plane is needed at EVERY pyramid level, not once: ~51000 B over a
    four-level pyramid, a FIFTH plane on top of the four the covariance
    already reads -- +25% of the derivative working set, held for the
    frame's lifetime.

